What the backend supplies

the atmosphere (tas, pr) for chion or smbpal, or the surface mass balance directly;
the ocean at the shelf base (T_shlf, S_shlf and their anomalies), interpolated from the reference ocean with the marine-shelf parameters, so step_shelf passes it straight to the marine shelf;
subglacial discharge Qd, landed on Yelmo by couple_to_yelmo.

Usage
scripts/run_chunks.sh [options] PAR OUTDIR T0 T1 [T2 ...]
T0 T1 ... are the chunk boundaries in the time of the timeline group (relative time, calendar years or elapsed time, as the par file runs). Options:

-r BUNDLE: restart bundle of the first chunk;
-d JOBID: the first chunk waits for this job;
-p "k=v ...": overrides for all chunks; --p-first, --p-rest: for the first or the later chunks only;
-g GROUP: the timeline group (default: [ctrl] run_step);
-e EXE, -n NAME: runme executable alias, job-name prefix.

The script prints the job of each chunk and, on the last line, the job id and the final bundle of the chain, so a next stage can be chained to it with -d and -r.
